{"title":"Career Roadmap · Game Designer","role":"Game Designer","summary":"A Game Designer designs the rules, systems, mechanics, player experience and overall structure of a game.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Animation & Game Design"},"about":[{"label":"Degree–Career Alignment","text":"Excellent"},{"label":"Career Type","text":"Game Design + Player Experience + Systems + Story + Production"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"Game Design Intern / Junior Game Designer / Associate Game Designer"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"What Does a Game Designer Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer designs the rules, systems, mechanics, player experience and overall structure of a game."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is different from a Game Artist or Game Programmer."},{"type":"p","text":"A programmer builds the technical systems that make the game work, while a designer decides:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What the player can do"},{"text":"How the game should respond"},{"text":"How difficulty should progress"},{"text":"How rewards work"},{"text":"How levels should be structured"},{"text":"How players learn mechanics"},{"text":"How combat, economy or progression systems operate"},{"text":"How the game remains engaging"},{"text":"How player behaviour should influence design decisions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A modern Game Designer therefore combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Creativity","Psychology","Systems Thinking","Game Mechanics","Data","Storytelling","Technical Understanding"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"During B.Des"},{"text":"Game Design Intern, Level Design Intern, Game Design Trainee"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Game Designer, Associate Game Designer, Level Designer"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Game Designer, Systems Designer, Content Designer, Narrative Designer"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Game Designer, Senior Systems Designer, Lead Level Designer"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Lead Game Designer, Game Design Director, Creative Director"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Systems Designer, Level Designer, Narrative Designer, Combat Designer, Economy Designer, UX Designer, Technical Designer"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Game Designer” is a broad profession. At larger studios, design is divided into specialised roles."}]},{"heading":"What Does a Game Designer Actually Work On?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A game designer may work on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Game mechanics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Movement"},{"text":"Combat"},{"text":"Weapons"},{"text":"Abilities"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Crafting"},{"text":"Quests"},{"text":"Challenges"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Character progression"},{"text":"Skill trees"},{"text":"XP systems"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Multiplayer matchmaking"},{"text":"Resource management"},{"text":"Rewards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Level design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Level structure"},{"text":"Player navigation"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Enemy placement"},{"text":"Objectives"},{"text":"Checkpoints"},{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"Difficulty progression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Player experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Onboarding"},{"text":"Tutorials"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Player retention"}]}]},{"heading":"Game Design vs Game Development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Role","Main Responsibility"],"rows":[[{"text":"Game Designer"},{"text":"Rules, mechanics, systems and player experience"}],[{"text":"Game Programmer"},{"text":"Code and technical implementation"}],[{"text":"2D Game Artist"},{"text":"Characters, environments and visual assets"}],[{"text":"3D Artist"},{"text":"3D models and environments"}],[{"text":"Animator"},{"text":"Movement and animation"}],[{"text":"Technical Artist"},{"text":"Art + technology pipeline"}],[{"text":"Narrative Designer"},{"text":"Story, dialogue and narrative systems"}],[{"text":"Level Designer"},{"text":"Gameplay spaces and level flow"}],[{"text":"Game Producer"},{"text":"Schedule, people and delivery"}],[{"text":"QA/Game Tester"},{"text":"Finding and validating defects"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer should still understand basic programming and game-engine workflows, even if programming is not their primary profession."}]},{"heading":"Build Skills During B.Des","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Game Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Start by understanding why games are fun and how games communicate rules."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Player goals"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Challenge"},{"text":"Risk/reward"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Game genres"},{"text":"Player motivation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analyse existing games"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not only play games."},{"type":"p","text":"Deconstruct them."},{"type":"p","text":"For each game, analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Core loop"},{"text":"Player goal"},{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Tutorial"},{"text":"Level structure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a Game Design Analysis Journal."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse at least 20 games across different genres."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Game Engines + Prototyping","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should become capable of turning a design idea into a playable prototype."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn a game engine"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one primary engine:"},{"type":"p","text":"Unity or Unreal Engine."},{"type":"p","text":"For an animation/game-design student, learning one engine deeply is more valuable than superficially learning five."},{"type":"h","text":"Unity pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity Editor"},{"text":"Scenes"},{"text":"GameObjects"},{"text":"Components"},{"text":"Prefabs"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Colliders"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"UI"},{"text":"Audio"},{"text":"C# fundamentals"},{"text":"Scriptable Objects"},{"text":"Basic AI"},{"text":"Build/deployment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Unreal pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unreal Editor"},{"text":"Actors"},{"text":"Components"},{"text":"Blueprints"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Materials basics"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"UI"},{"text":"Gameplay systems"},{"text":"Basic C++"},{"text":"AI basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer does not need to become a full software engineer, but should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Conditions"},{"text":"Loops"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Objects"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Debugging"},{"text":"Basic algorithms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"C# for Unity or Blueprints/C++ for Unreal are valuable."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build small games rather than attempting a massive open-world game."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — 2D Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Player movement"},{"text":"Enemy"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Score"},{"text":"Basic progression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Gameplay Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"A player has three abilities with different cooldowns and must defeat increasingly difficult enemies."},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Combat"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Balancing"},{"text":"Progression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Game Mechanic Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Take one mechanic from an existing game and redesign it."},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Original mechanic","Problem","Proposed change","Prototype","Playtest","Results"]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Advanced Game Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should develop a professional design mindset."},{"type":"h","text":"Systems design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Progression systems"},{"text":"Skill trees"},{"text":"XP systems"},{"text":"Currency"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Crafting"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Difficulty curves"},{"text":"Character progression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Level design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Player flow"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Spatial composition"},{"text":"Encounter design"},{"text":"Environmental storytelling"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Landmarks"},{"text":"Difficulty progression"},{"text":"Checkpoints"},{"text":"Level metrics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game balancing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Damage"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Enemy scaling"},{"text":"Weapon statistics"},{"text":"Drop rates"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"XP curves"},{"text":"Resource scarcity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use spreadsheets extensively."},{"type":"p","text":"Excel/Google Sheets is a surprisingly important Game Design tool."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Specialisation + Professional Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose a primary specialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Track A — Systems Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Character systems"},{"text":"Balancing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track B — Level Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Level layout"},{"text":"Gameplay spaces"},{"text":"Encounters"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Pacing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track C — Narrative Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Characters"},{"text":"Quests"},{"text":"Narrative systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track D — Combat Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weapons"},{"text":"Combat mechanics"},{"text":"Enemy behaviour"},{"text":"Abilities"},{"text":"Boss design"},{"text":"Difficulty"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track E — Game UX Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tutorials"},{"text":"HUD"},{"text":"Menus"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Player feedback"},{"text":"Onboarding"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track F — Technical Game Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gameplay scripting"},{"text":"Tools"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Game systems"},{"text":"Designer-engineer collaboration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly valuable for candidates who enjoy both design and programming."}]},{"heading":"Four-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Focus","Expected Output"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Game analysis + mechanics"},{"text":"20 game analyses"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Engine + prototyping"},{"text":"2–4 playable prototypes"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Systems + level design"},{"text":"2–3 substantial projects"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Specialisation + team project"},{"text":"1 polished game + professional portfolio"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Job readiness"},{"text":"4–6 strong design case studies"}]]}]},{"heading":"Core Game Design Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Game Mechanics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Core loops"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Actions"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Challenges"},{"text":"Risk/reward"},{"text":"Failure states"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Systems Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"XP"},{"text":"Resources"},{"text":"Crafting"},{"text":"Skill trees"},{"text":"Character statistics"},{"text":"Balancing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Level Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spatial design"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Encounter design"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Environmental storytelling"},{"text":"Difficulty curves"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Player Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Flow"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Curiosity"},{"text":"Mastery"},{"text":"Competition"},{"text":"Cooperation"},{"text":"Reward systems"}]}]},{"heading":"Technical Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Unity or Unreal"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"C# / Blueprint"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Game prototyping"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Game balancing"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Excel/Sheets"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"3D basics"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Animation basics"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"UI/UX"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Audio implementation"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Python and SQL are not mandatory for entry-level Game Design, but they become useful for player analytics and live-service games."}]},{"heading":"Game Design Documentation","kind":"other","block