n"},{"text":"Team collaboration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"At minimum:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1 polished playable game"},{"text":"1 level design project"},{"text":"1 systems-design project"},{"text":"1 game-economy/balancing project"},{"text":"1 UX/playtesting project"},{"text":"1 team-developed game"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A playable build or interactive prototype should accompany the portfolio wherever possible."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Animation & Game Design","Learn Game Mechanics + Player Psychology","Master Unity or Unreal Engine","Learn C#/Blueprint + Basic Programming","Build Small Playable Prototypes","Learn Level Design + Systems Design + Game Balancing","Conduct Real Player Playtests","Build 4–6 Strong Game Design Case Studies","Complete 1–2 Game Studio/Indie Internships","Participate in Game Jams and Team Projects","Apply for Game Design / Level Design / Associate Game Designer Roles","Game Designer","Specialise in Systems / Level / Combat / Narrative / UX / Technical Design","Senior Designer → Lead Designer → Design Director / Creative Director"]},{"type":"note","label":"Overall Assessment","text":"Excellent"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Des in Animation & Game Design is a highly direct foundation for Game Designer. The biggest differentiator is not simply knowing a game engine—it is demonstrating that you can design mechanics, balance systems, create playable prototypes, conduct player testing and iterate based on evidence. A graduate who combines those abilities with basic programming, game analytics and AI-assisted development will have a significantly stronger profile for the evolving game industry."}]}]}